  "worked_solution": "To raise a power to another power, we simply multiply the exponents:\n\n$$\n{({(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2})}^{-4}={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2\\cdot (-4)}={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-8}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate ${(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-8},$ we find the reciprocal of the base $\\frac{1}{2}$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-8}={2}^{8}=256\n$$",
